# ── Runtime data, never build input ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WORKSPACE_DIR=/app/workspace and BACKUP_DIR=/app/backups are EFS mounts at
# run time. On a developer machine the same paths fill up with real project
# scaffolding - 1,415 entries here - and none of it belongs in an image.
#
# Left out, this is not merely wasteful. The scaffolding is COPY'd into the
# build stage, some of it is traced into .next/standalone, and it ships inside
# the layer where the EFS mount then hides it: present in the artifact,
# invisible from the running container. The containment assertion in
# docker/web.Dockerfile is what caught it, by finding two
# workspace/<uuid>/docker-compose.yml files that survived the exclusion sweep.
#
# It was also most of the build: excluding these cuts the context transfer from
# minutes to seconds.
workspace
backups
tmp

# Every env file. The build takes its public values as --build-arg (see
# scripts/verify-public-build-inputs.ts) and needs none of these; .env and
# .env.local were already excluded, while .env.vercel and .env.bak-rotate were
# not, and were being sent to the daemon.
.env*
!.env.example

